{"body":"Hi @Soph , this pr addresses #1877 out-of-scope documentation fix. Would appreciate your review on this. Thanks!","user":"MuskanPaliwal"}
{"body":"Verified every entry against the source - an `As*` helper in `capabilities.go` is ungated exactly when it resolves by bare type assertion rather than `declaredCapability[T]`, which is 10 helpers. The list goes from 5/10 to 9/10 with this change, and all four additions are correct. `SessionEndBudgeter` wasn't in the review note you cited, so that one's a genuine find on top of the ask (the PR body says \"three interfaces\" but the diff adds four - worth reconciling).\n\n**One still missing: `ToolInvocationScanner`** (`capabilities.go:230`). It belongs between `SkillEventExtractor` and `SessionEndBudgeter`, which is exactly where the gap is in declaration order.\n\nNot really your miss, though: `AsToolInvocationScanner` landed on 2026-08-24 in `a1dd3efc3`, after this PR was opened but before it merged main on the 26th. The list went stale again inside the lifetime of the fix for staleness.\n\nWhich is the more useful thing here. This list is hand-maintained with no sync mechanism and has now rotted twice, and all 10 ungated helpers already carry their own, more detailed rationale next to the code - `AsHookFreshness` explains the template-based drift, `AsSessionEndBudgeter` explains the parse","user":"Soph"}
{"body":"Thanks @Soph, good catch. I went with the AST-backed option.\n\nThe follow-up commit makes every package-level `As*` helper use either `builtinCapability` or `declaredCapability`. The test scans production files across the top-level `agent` package, so it catches helpers outside `capabilities.go`, including `AsContextInjector` and `AsModelLister`. It derives the built-in set from those helpers and checks that the `DeclaredCaps` list matches it exactly and stays alphabetized.\n\nI also added `ToolInvocationScanner` and characterization tests for the four normalized helpers. Their signatures, return values, and declaration behavior are unchanged.\n\nThe guard currently covers all 23 `As*` helpers, 13 built-in and 10 declaration-gated, without hard-coding those counts. `mise run check` passes. I also removed `ToolInvocationScanner` from the documentation temporarily and confirmed that the test failed with the expected mismatch.\n\nI’ve updated the PR description to match the new scope.\n","user":"MuskanPaliwal"}
{"body":"hi @Soph , i have this open for a long, would love to get your feedback here and get it merged . thanks :))","user":"MuskanPaliwal"}
{"body":"@cursoragent review\r\n","user":"MuskanPaliwal"}
